# Styling & NativeWind — fieldops-app

This app is a NativeWind **host**. The UI library ships class strings and a preset; this repo wires the engine.

## Feasibility law

| Claim | Verdict |
| --- | --- |
| NativeWind `className` on RN | Works when **this host** wires NativeWind |
| Tailwind utilities without NativeWind on RN | Impossible |
| Invent a second app colour theme | Forbidden — FieldOps tokens / UI preset only |

## Host duties

1. Install `nativewind` v4 + peers (`tailwindcss@^3`, reanimated, safe-area per NW docs).
2. Babel + Metro (`withNativeWind`) + `global.css`.
3. `presets: [require('nativewind/preset'), require('@pranadwaghmare2/fieldops-ui/preset')]`.
4. `content` includes app/src paths **and** `./node_modules/@pranadwaghmare2/fieldops-ui/lib/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}`.
5. Screens use components from `core/integrations/ui` — not a parallel design system.

## Theme

- Visual tokens come from the UI preset + `src/core/theme` (same numbers).
- No dark mode, no custom fonts, no shadows — hairline borders and radius 10 per brief.
- Do not add Emotion, styled-components, or a third styling system.

## Feature code

- Features do not import `nativewind` directly. Host wiring lives in integrations/styling + root config files.
- Prefer library components’ `className` / `style` props for overrides.
